  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39613044",
      "title": "Installing Ubuntu [VirtualBox]",
      "lectureOrder": 9,
      "videoOrder": 6,
      "sourceHash": "e80cd1b976bee7bf5eba78f19f74000617928a58e1fb5e7f2bbfbb5be9747925",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at how we can install Ubuntu and to install ubuntu in our VirtualBox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "We need to download the Ubuntu desktop image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 14.37,
          "en": "This image contains the whole operating system, including an installer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "So usually if we still had a computer with a DVD drive we would burn it on a DVD and then boot from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "that DVD and then we could install that on a real computer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "Or nowadays usually we do not have a DVD drive anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "Then we would need to put it on a USB drive and then boot from that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "However, we do not want to install ubuntu on a real computer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "We want to install it on our virtual computer and luckily VirtualBox can take care of this install procedure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "So all that we need to do is that we need to go to ubuntu.com and download the latest desktop image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "Important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 53.76,
          "en": "We will be using the LTS version of ubuntu in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "LTS stands for long term support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 62.53,
          "en": "Usually in ubuntu version is released every six months, but every two years they are releasing an LTS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.53,
          "end": 68.71000000000001,
          "en": "version of ubuntu that is supported for a longer period of time and this allows me to have a more stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.74,
          "end": 75.73,
          "en": "base so that I don't need to update my course every six months and only every two years.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 75.73,
          "end": 77.23,
          "en": "There's a new version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 77.23,
          "end": 81.31,
          "en": "If there's a new version you can just use that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 81.31,
          "end": 86.86,
          "en": "If there are any differences, I will have added text lectures here in this course or I will have changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 86.86,
          "end": 88.18,
          "en": "the videos accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.18,
          "end": 89.92,
          "en": "So this course is up to date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.92,
          "end": 95.62,
          "en": "Even if here in this video, I'm still working with the previous version, so I will be using the latest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 96.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.32,
          "en": "version of ubuntu in this course and you can do to whatever is the latest version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 101.32,
          "end": 103.24000000000001,
          "en": "Let's just have a look at this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 103.24000000000001,
          "end": 109.21000000000001,
          "en": "And for this we need to go on the website of ubuntu and then we can just click download and then we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 109.21000000000001,
          "end": 110.97999999999999,
          "en": "want to download Ubuntu desktop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 110.97999999999999,
          "end": 111.97,
          "en": "So I click here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 111.97,
          "end": 117.4,
          "en": "Then I need to scroll down a little bit and then I want to download the latest version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 117.4,
          "end": 120.37,
          "en": "This would be 22.04.3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 120.37,
          "end": 121.24,
          "en": "As of now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 121.24,
          "end": 125.02,
          "en": "Again, probably a more recent version when you will be watching this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 125.02,
          "end": 130.12,
          "en": "But again, one if there would be any changes, this course would be adapted to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 130.12,
          "end": 134.62,
          "en": "So now we can see the download it will take here in this case about a minute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 134.71,
          "end": 136.48,
          "en": "It depends on your internet connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 136.48,
          "end": 138.04,
          "en": "So I will now just wait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 138.46,
          "end": 145.12,
          "en": "Now that this image has finished downloading, I can go back into my VirtualBox here and I want to now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 145.12,
          "end": 147.76,
          "en": "create a new virtual machine for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 147.76,
          "end": 153.52,
          "en": "I switch to the welcome screen here and then I just click new to create a new virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.52,
          "end": 161.38,
          "en": "I will call my virtual machine ubuntu LTS by the way, in case this menu here looks different on your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 161.38,
          "end": 162.04,
          "en": "machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 162.07,
          "end": 163.81,
          "en": "There's an expert mode here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 163.81,
          "end": 165.1,
          "en": "Maybe it looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 165.13,
          "end": 168.43,
          "en": "If it looks like this then you can just click on guided mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 168.43,
          "end": 170.71,
          "en": "This one is definitely enough for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.82999999999998,
          "end": 171.97,
          "en": "Now we want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 172.27,
          "end": 173.5,
          "en": "I need to type it in again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.53,
          "end": 175.54,
          "en": "I will call it Ubuntu LTS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.54,
          "end": 182.35,
          "en": "And what I want to do now is that I need to click, I need to select an ISO image first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 182.35,
          "end": 188.71,
          "en": "So for this I now select other here and I go into my downloads folder and I just select my iso.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.95,
          "end": 193.15,
          "en": "Then I want to tick this checkbox here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.42,
          "end": 200.82999999999998,
          "en": "This is extremely important because otherwise VirtualBox will try to install everything for us, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 200.82999999999998,
          "end": 203.59,
          "en": "by doing that it will do some problems or errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 203.59,
          "end": 204.01,
          "en": "Here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 204.01,
          "end": 207.19,
          "en": "For example, the language settings weren't configured properly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 207.19,
          "end": 214.75,
          "en": "This would prevent apps such as the Terminal from launching and the user wouldn't be configured correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.75,
          "end": 220.99,
          "en": "If you have used Linux before, the user would be configured in a way that sudo doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 220.99,
          "end": 224.14,
          "en": "If you have never used Linux before, don't worry about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 224.17000000000002,
          "end": 226.84,
          "en": "We will get to this later here in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 226.84,
          "end": 231.31,
          "en": "Just one more word about this checkbox in case you are unable to tick this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 231.31,
          "end": 232.84,
          "en": "That's totally all right as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 232.84,
          "end": 236.02,
          "en": "In this case, automatic install isn't an option here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 236.29,
          "end": 238.18,
          "en": "That happens from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 238.18,
          "end": 241.9,
          "en": "So if you can tick this checkbox, be sure to tick it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 241.9,
          "end": 244.12,
          "en": "If you can't, that's all right as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 244.21,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "So let's now continue by clicking on next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 247.3,
          "end": 250.84,
          "en": "Now we need to configure our virtual computer here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 250.84,
          "end": 254.29,
          "en": "In this case, it suggests 2000MB of memory here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 254.29,
          "end": 260.53,
          "en": "In my case, I have way enough memory here on my system so I can just give it significantly more memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 260.53,
          "end": 264.76,
          "en": "But anything above 512 should already be enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 264.76,
          "end": 270.13,
          "en": "One gigabyte would also would be better if you can spare two gigabytes, that would be great here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 270.13,
          "end": 275.83,
          "en": "In my case, I don't need to care about this so I can allocate quite a bit of memory to this machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 275.83,
          "end": 282.46,
          "en": "Also here, how many CPU cores do you want to allocate to this machine or up to so many CPU cores it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 282.46,
          "end": 283.27,
          "en": "can then use?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 283.27,
          "end": 290.47,
          "en": "Also here, in my case, I recommend 2 or 4 if you can spare them and this should then definitely be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 290.47,
          "end": 290.95,
          "en": "enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 290.95,
          "end": 292.18,
          "en": "Then I click next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 292.21,
          "end": 295.27,
          "en": "We now also need to create a virtual hard disk here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 295.27,
          "end": 299.2,
          "en": "In this case, 25GB is actually a little bit at the lower end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 299.2,
          "end": 300.19,
          "en": "I recommend something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 300.19,
          "end": 303.48,
          "en": "Like 100GB, at least here in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 303.49,
          "end": 308.53,
          "en": "The way it works is that the hard drive only needs space if we actually use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 308.53,
          "end": 311.56,
          "en": "So we can just create it with 100GB for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 311.56,
          "end": 317.35,
          "en": "And this hard drive will be a file on our Windows computer here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 317.71,
          "end": 323.11,
          "en": "And this file will only grow in size when our virtual machine actually needs that space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 323.11,
          "end": 326.53,
          "en": "So it doesn't hurt to use a larger number here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 326.62,
          "end": 332.2,
          "en": "The next thing is that I can just click next and then finish and now this virtual machine will boot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 332.2,
          "end": 335.35,
          "en": "and I can now see if everything works here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 335.35,
          "end": 338.92,
          "en": "So now we can see it's powered off and I now need to start it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 341.17,
          "en": "It doesn't start automatically, never mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 341.2,
          "end": 343.69,
          "en": "So now the virtual machine is booting up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 343.69,
          "end": 346.54,
          "en": "I got like several of those messages here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 346.54,
          "end": 347.56,
          "en": "Just confirm with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 347.59000000000003,
          "end": 348.19,
          "en": "Yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 349.08,
          "end": 353.19,
          "en": "And then at some point we are here in our virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 353.19,
          "end": 357.87,
          "en": "By the way, once you click into that, your cursor might hide in order to return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 357.93,
          "end": 364.41,
          "en": "The default configuration is Ctrl and Alt, and you need to press those two keys at the same time and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 364.41,
          "end": 366.26,
          "en": "then your cursor is back in windows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 366.27,
          "end": 371.73,
          "en": "I had to change it here because my windows machine is in another room and I'm just connecting it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 371.73,
          "end": 375.81,
          "en": "Also, you can also go into the settings here to change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 375.81,
          "end": 384.78,
          "en": "That would be in the preferences and then through input and then virtual machine, you could change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 384.78,
          "end": 390.9,
          "en": "this host key combination to something else in case you are not able to press those keys properly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 391.05,
          "end": 391.74,
          "en": "Nevermind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 391.77,
          "end": 397.32,
          "en": "Nonetheless, if I now once I click now here you can see my mouse is now locked and I'm now connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 397.32,
          "end": 401.25,
          "en": "directly here to this virtual computer to go out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 401.25,
          "end": 406.92,
          "en": "In this case here, I just need to press this key again that I selected there or Ctrl and Alt, depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 406.92,
          "end": 408.73,
          "en": "on the default configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 408.73,
          "end": 415.12,
          "en": "Now I want to select try or install ubuntu and now here my ubuntu should boot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 415.62,
          "end": 416.77,
          "en": "So here we are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 416.79,
          "end": 420.87,
          "en": "First, I will now close this menu and we are now here in an install menu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 420.87,
          "end": 426.93,
          "en": "I now want to install ubuntu here, so I click on install ubuntu and I now click through this install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 426.93,
          "end": 427.44,
          "en": "guide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 427.47,
          "end": 429.87,
          "en": "The first option here is the keyboard layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 429.87,
          "end": 433.29,
          "en": "I highly recommend you to be really careful here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 433.71,
          "end": 437.88,
          "en": "So here you can choose the keyboard layout that you want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 437.88,
          "end": 445.98,
          "en": "And for example on my case I'm used to the German keyboard layout, so I should look o not detect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 445.98,
          "end": 448.02,
          "en": "and need to click through here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 448.26,
          "end": 450.51,
          "en": "Um, let's see where we find German here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 450.51,
          "end": 453.75,
          "en": "In my case, I need the German and the Macintosh keyboard here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 453.75,
          "end": 459.3,
          "en": "In your case, this will probably be something different, but really be sure that that you select the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 459.3,
          "end": 464.43,
          "en": "right one here, because otherwise, uh, different symbols might not work as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 464.43,
          "end": 467.15999999999997,
          "en": "So here in my case, I do need to select this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 467.25,
          "end": 472.77,
          "en": "And the next thing is that I want to select here is that I want to do a normal install and I also want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 472.77,
          "end": 479.61,
          "en": "to install all the updates already while installing Ubuntu third party software for graphics and additional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 479.61,
